<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion (Mammuthus primigenius tusk (Museum Wiesbaden); Monodon monoceros tusk (torsion analogue))",
        "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion faithfully reproduces Mammuthus primigenius tusk (Museum Wiesbaden); Monodon monoceros tusk (torsion analogue) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-032-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-032-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-032-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-032-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mammuthus primigenius tusk (Museum Wiesbaden); Monodon monoceros tusk (torsion analogue) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py> ;
    schema:about "Mammuthus primigenius tusk (Museum Wiesbaden); Monodon monoceros tusk (torsion analogue)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: No growth-rate (v_max, v_min) or CT data: λ = 0.862 and Δ = 0.148 are inferred from the fitted geometry, not measured",
        "does_not_claim: No handedness determination from the narwhal photograph (tip orientation unknown); along-shaft tan α trend is confounded by camera obliquity and not scored",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic accretion law κ = (v_max − v_min)/(w v̄) = Δ/w and its gnomonic closure tan ψ = Δ/c_s (arc-length taper) ⇔ sin ψ = Δ/c_r (E4-E5), verified against the integrated ODE (r = 1.000)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Kiladze chord ratio tan α = π/(2 tan φ) conversion from a locally measured groove inclination (E7)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Screw-accretion frame update Ω = κ b + τ n generating circle / log spiral / helix / helico-spiral (E6), fitted in 3-D to the projected specimen centreline",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 619, 633-634: constant growth-rate ratio across the basal zone yields a logarithmic spiral; tooth, tusk, beak, claw all follow it; elephant tusk tip ~ spiral pole; long tusks (mammoth, Babirussa) are curves of double curvature",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 621-623 + Fig. 321: St Venant torsion warps non-circular prisms into anticlastic surfaces whose contour lines explain the sinuous growth lines of trihedral horns",
        "transfer_boundary: A single 2-D museum photograph projects a 3-D helico-spiral tusk; the 3-D fit recovers view angles but the broken root inflates w(s) and the tip hook is foreshortened",
        "transfer_boundary: The narwhal tusk is a labelled analogue for the torsion component; Thompson's 1917 chapter never names the narwhal" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py; output: docs/media/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png; organism: Mammuthus primigenius tusk (Museum Wiesbaden); Monodon monoceros tusk (torsion analogue); environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 619, 633-634: constant growth-rate ratio across the basal zone yields a logarithmic spiral; tooth, tusk, beak, claw all follow it; elephant tusk tip ~ spiral pole; long tusks (mammoth, Babirussa) are curves of double curvature | Thompson pp. 621-623 + Fig. 321: St Venant torsion warps non-circular prisms into anticlastic surfaces whose contour lines explain the sinuous growth lines of trihedral horns; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic accretion law κ = (v_max − v_min)/(w v̄) = Δ/w and its gnomonic closure tan ψ = Δ/c_s (arc-length taper) ⇔ sin ψ = Δ/c_r (E4-E5), verified against the integrated ODE (r = 1.000) | Screw-accretion frame update Ω = κ b + τ n generating circle / log spiral / helix / helico-spiral (E6), fitted in 3-D to the projected specimen centreline | Kiladze chord ratio tan α = π/(2 tan φ) conversion from a locally measured groove inclination (E7); transfer_boundary: The narwhal tusk is a labelled analogue for the torsion component; Thompson's 1917 chapter never names the narwhal | A single 2-D museum photograph projects a 3-D helico-spiral tusk; the 3-D fit recovers view angles but the broken root inflates w(s) and the tip hook is foreshortened; does_not_claim: No growth-rate (v_max, v_min) or CT data: λ = 0.862 and Δ = 0.148 are inferred from the fitted geometry, not measured | No handedness determination from the narwhal photograph (tip orientation unknown); along-shaft tan α trend is confounded by camera obliquity and not scored]; other sources: On Growth and Form <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Mémoire sur la torsion des prismes, avec des considérations sur leur flexion <https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k99739w>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dib.2018.09.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.14430/arctic1723>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/1301992> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-032-the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-tee-audit-v2-thompson1917-t1917-032-1>,
