    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — MorphoEval overall 86.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py` (overall ~86.0/100, up from 60.7 in v1). The remediated script fits the full 3-D screw-accretion model to the segmented mammoth tusk (constant-width twisted helix RMSE 17.4 px vs plane 33.1 px, ΔAIC 477; measured-width law 23.1 vs 37.3 px, ΔAIC 355), sweeps 30 (λ, c) + 5 τ + 16 ψ regimes confirming every Lean-proved monotonicity and the E5 closure (r = 1.000, RMSE 0.2°), adds Archimedean / shuffled-width / τ = 0 / circular-section controls, block-bootstrap CIs and a one-sample KS test, measures the narwhal groove angle (φ = 29.5°, 95% CI 26.3-33.0° → α ≡ 70.2° vs 66.9 ± 3.3° published, z = +1.00) and reproduces the six-sector St Venant torsion curves of Fig. 321. Verdict MIXED: torsion / double curvature supported, gnomonic accretion log spiral not supported on this projection. Overall 86.0/100 (faithfulness 84.6, reproducibility 89.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3ae9ce99c; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py at 3ae9ce99c, image/png, 1014396 B, 2205×1953 px, artifact_sha256 e154f28e16ab5cbcdb1a2d11cbfb0139e8113445b8812d87ff767241c3186ebb (sha256 e154f28e16ab5cbcdb1a2d11cbfb0139e8113445b8812d87ff767241c3186ebb), spec_fingerprint 414a4dcdfdb8857b568651bc291ee292368ae1a49e5e1fb3b1d8e880d3f1ae7f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 414a4dcdfdb8857b568651bc291ee292368ae1a49e5e1fb3b1d8e880d3f1ae7f; artifact_sha256: e154f28e16ab5cbcdb1a2d11cbfb0139e8113445b8812d87ff767241c3186ebb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/kiladze2018_narwhal_spiral_table1.csv=f1e9d5a363772f32..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/mammuthus_primigenius_tusk_specimen.jpg=cd33e02d49367204..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/monodon_monoceros_tusk_spiral_specimen.jpg=3c0e4ccdd686c45b..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_reference.json=29f81480c8dea387...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-032-the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-tee-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 619, 633-634: constant growth-rate ratio across the basal zone yields a logarithmic spiral; tooth, tusk, beak, claw all follow it; elephant tusk tip ~ spiral pole; long tusks (mammoth, Babirussa) are curves of double curvature | Thompson pp. 621-623 + Fig. 321: St Venant torsion warps non-circular prisms into anticlastic surfaces whose contour lines explain the sinuous growth lines of trihedral horns; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic accretion law κ = (v_max − v_min)/(w v̄) = Δ/w and its gnomonic closure tan ψ = Δ/c_s (arc-length taper) ⇔ sin ψ = Δ/c_r (E4-E5), verified against the integrated ODE (r = 1.000) | Screw-accretion frame update Ω = κ b + τ n generating circle / log spiral / helix / helico-spiral (E6), fitted in 3-D to the projected specimen centreline | Kiladze chord ratio tan α = π/(2 tan φ) conversion from a locally measured groove inclination (E7); transfer_boundary: The narwhal tusk is a labelled analogue for the torsion component; Thompson's 1917 chapter never names the narwhal | A single 2-D museum photograph projects a 3-D helico-spiral tusk; the 3-D fit recovers view angles but the broken root inflates w(s) and the tip hook is foreshortened; does_not_claim: No growth-rate (v_max, v_min) or CT data: λ = 0.862 and Δ = 0.148 are inferred from the fitted geometry, not measured | No handedness determination from the narwhal photograph (tip orientation unknown); along-shaft tan α trend is confounded by camera obliquity and not scored." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Acquire a second, intact mammoth or elephant tusk photograph (or a CT centreline) to test the accretion width-law κ ∝ 1/w(s) without the broken-root bias, and fit the screw model jointly to two views to resolve the 3-D helico-spiral directly.",
        "remediation needed: Measure Kiladze-style chord angles on several narwhal tusks with known tip orientation to test the uniform-torsion prediction tan α ∝ 1/d free of camera obliquity, and record handedness." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

