<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "HSV segmentation + skeleton longest path (`segment_mammoth_tusk`, `tusk_centreline_profile`, L300-L386) recovers the SHA-256-locked mammoth centreline and width; the fitted twisted screw model tracks the whole tusk including the reversed tip hook at RMSE 17.4 px (~1.1 % of the 1.5 kpx arc; overlay in panel (a), growth GIF panel 3). The narwhal groove orientation field is extracted by structure tensor in the low-foreshortening strip (L702-L745) and the computed St Venant contours are overlaid on Thompson's own Fig. 321 crop. Deductions: the accretion width-law fit (23.1 px) is worse than the constant-width helix, the root is broken (inflated w(s)), the narwhal is an analogue, and the 3-D form is judged in 2-D only." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
